# Strategy & Template Backend API + Frontend Integration

Implement the 7 empty backend feature stubs (DuplicateStrategy + 6 Template operations) following the established MediatR + Carter + FluentValidation pattern, then wire the frontend [trade-context.tsx](file:///c:/project/.NET/v0-trading-journey-app/lib/trade-context.tsx) to call these APIs instead of using local state.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend — DuplicateStrategy

#### [MODIFY] [DuplicateStrategy.cs](file:///c:/project/.NET/TradingJournal/modules/Strategies/TradingJournal.Modules.Strategies/Features/V1/Stategies/DuplicateStrategy.cs)

- **Request**: `ICommand<Result<int>>` with `int Id`
- **Validator**: `Id > 0`
- **Handler**: Fetch strategy by ID, clone all fields, append `" (Copy)"` to name, set `Status = Draft`, reset `Id = 0`, add & save
- **Endpoint**: `POST api/v1/strategies/{id}/duplicate` → returns `201 Created` with new ID

---

### Backend — Template CRUD

All template endpoints use route group `api/v1/strategy-templates` and `Tags.StrategyTemplate`.

#### [MODIFY] [CreateTemplete.cs](file:///c:/project/.NET/TradingJournal/modules/Strategies/TradingJournal.Modules.Strategies/Features/V1/Templetes/CreateTemplete.cs)

- **Request**: Record with all template config fields (Name, Description, Category, Asset, Timeframe, DateRange, Indicators, Risk params)
- **Validator**: Name + Asset + Timeframe required
- **Handler**: Map to [StrategyTemplate](file:///c:/project/.NET/v0-trading-journey-app/lib/playbook-store.ts#296-304) entity, serialize indicator lists as JSON, save to DB
- **Endpoint**: `POST /` → `201 Created`

#### [MODIFY] [DeleteTemplete.cs](file:///c:/project/.NET/TradingJournal/modules/Strategies/TradingJournal.Modules.Strategies/Features/V1/Templetes/DeleteTemplete.cs)

- **Request**: `ICommand<Result<int>>` with `int Id`
- **Handler**: Find by ID, remove, save
- **Endpoint**: `DELETE /{id}` → `200 OK`

#### [MODIFY] [GetTempletes.cs](file:///c:/project/.NET/TradingJournal/modules/Strategies/TradingJournal.Modules.Strategies/Features/V1/Templetes/GetTempletes.cs)

- **Request**: Empty `IQuery<Result<List<TemplateViewModel>>>`
- **Handler**: Query all templates, map to [TemplateViewModel](file:///c:/project/.NET/TradingJournal/modules/Strategies/TradingJournal.Modules.Strategies/ViewModel/TemplateViewModel.cs#3-23) with JSON-deserialized indicators
- **Endpoint**: `GET /` → `200 OK`

#### [MODIFY] [GetTempleteDetails.cs](file:///c:/project/.NET/TradingJournal/modules/Strategies/TradingJournal.Modules.Strategies/Features/V1/Templetes/GetTempleteDetails.cs)

- **Request**: `IQuery<Result<TemplateDetailViewModel>>` with `int Id`
- **Validator**: `Id > 0`
- **Handler**: Find by ID, map to [TemplateDetailViewModel](file:///c:/project/.NET/TradingJournal/modules/Strategies/TradingJournal.Modules.Strategies/ViewModel/TemplateDetailViewModel.cs#3-41)
- **Endpoint**: `GET /{id}` → `200 OK` or `400`

#### [MODIFY] [UpdateTemplete.cs](file:///c:/project/.NET/TradingJournal/modules/Strategies/TradingJournal.Modules.Strategies/Features/V1/Templetes/UpdateTemplete.cs)

- **Request**: Record with `Id` + all config fields
- **Validator**: `Id > 0`, `Name` not empty
- **Handler**: Find by ID, update all fields, save
- **Endpoint**: `PUT /{id}` → `200 OK`

#### [MODIFY] [LoadAndBackTestTemplete.cs](file:///c:/project/.NET/TradingJournal/modules/Strategies/TradingJournal.Modules.Strategies/Features/V1/Templetes/LoadAndBackTestTemplete.cs)

- **Request**: `ICommand<Result<int>>` with `int TemplateId`
- **Validator**: `TemplateId > 0`
- **Handler**: Fetch template, create a new [Strategy](file:///c:/project/.NET/TradingJournal/modules/Strategies/TradingJournal.Modules.Strategies/Domain/Strategy.cs#7-66) entity from its config (name = template name, status = Draft), save the strategy
- **Endpoint**: `POST /{id}/load-and-backtest` → `201 Created` with new strategy ID

---

### Frontend — API Integration

#### [MODIFY] [trade-context.tsx](file:///c:/project/.NET/v0-trading-journey-app/lib/trade-context.tsx)

Replace local-only operations with API calls for strategies and templates:

| Function | API Call | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| [addStrategy](file:///c:/project/.NET/v0-trading-journey-app/lib/trade-context.tsx#170-179) | `POST /v1/strategies` | Map enums (string→int before send, int→string on receive) |
| [updateStrategy](file:///c:/project/.NET/v0-trading-journey-app/lib/trade-context.tsx#180-185) | `PUT /v1/strategies/{id}` | Same enum mapping |
| [deleteStrategy](file:///c:/project/.NET/v0-trading-journey-app/lib/trade-context.tsx#186-189) | `DELETE /v1/strategies/{id}` | |
| [duplicateStrategy](file:///c:/project/.NET/v0-trading-journey-app/lib/trade-context.tsx#225-240) | `POST /v1/strategies/{id}/duplicate` | Refetch strategies after |
| [saveTemplate](file:///c:/project/.NET/v0-trading-journey-app/lib/trade-context.tsx#212-220) | `POST /v1/strategy-templates` | Map category string→enum int |
| [deleteTemplate](file:///c:/project/.NET/v0-trading-journey-app/lib/trade-context.tsx#221-224) | `DELETE /v1/strategy-templates/{id}` | |

Add `useEffect` hooks to load strategies and templates from the API on mount:
- `GET /v1/strategies` → map to `PlaybookStrategy[]`
- `GET /v1/strategy-templates` → map to `StrategyTemplate[]` (custom templates only)

**Enum mapping** between frontend strings and backend integers:

| Frontend | Backend Enum |
|---|---|
| `"backtest"` / `"forward"` | `StrategyType` (0, 1) |
| `"draft"` / `"running"` / `"completed"` | `StrategyStatus` (0, 1, 2) |
| `"fixed"` / `"atr"` / `"percent"` | [StopLossType](file:///c:/project/.NET/v0-trading-journey-app/app/constants/playbook.ts#3-4) (0, 1, 2) |
| `"fixed"` / `"rr-ratio"` / `"percent"` | [TakeProfitType](file:///c:/project/.NET/v0-trading-journey-app/app/constants/playbook.ts#4-5) (0, 1, 2) |
| `"fixed"` / `"percent-equity"` | [PositionSizingType](file:///c:/project/.NET/v0-trading-journey-app/app/constants/playbook.ts#5-6) (0, 1) |
| `"scalping"` / `"swing"` / `"position"` / `"day-trading"` / `"custom"` | `StrategyCategory` (0, 1, 2, 3, 4) |

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Build Check
```bash
cd c:\project\.NET\TradingJournal
dotnet build
```
This validates that all 7 backend files compile with the correct MediatR/Carter patterns.

### Manual Verification
1. Run backend (`dotnet run`), open Swagger UI at `https://localhost:7177/swagger`
2. Test each template endpoint: Create → Get all → Get details → Update → Delete
3. Test duplicate strategy endpoint
4. Run frontend (`npm run dev`), verify strategies and templates load from API
5. Create a strategy via the builder, confirm it persists after page refresh
6. Save as template, then delete the template
7. Use "Load & Backtest" on a template, confirm a new strategy is created
